{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af16331","nodeId":"fRl4EfNwlBiidzn3IV34-","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# cgroups\n\ncgroups (control groups) are Linux kernel features that limit and manage system resources like CPU, memory, and I/O for process groups. Docker uses cgroups to enforce resource constraints on containers, ensuring predictable performance and preventing containers from consuming excessive system resources.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Control Groups","url":"https://www.docker.com/resources/what-container/#control-groups","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbad4"},{"type":"article","title":"Control Groups - Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@furkan.turkal/how-does-docker-actually-work-the-hard-way-a-technical-deep-diving-c5b8ea2f0422","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbad5"},{"type":"video","title":"An introduction to cgroups, runc & containerD","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1LeMndEk70","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dbad6"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/fRl4EfNwlBiidzn3IV34-.md"}